Meeting Minutes (MoM)

Project Review Meeting – John’s Requirements & Action Items

Objective: Capture the key expectations, requests, and decisions made by John during the meeting.

⸻

1. Knowledge Base & AI Workflow

Requirement

* Build an MCP Wrapper for the Knowledge Base so AI agents can automatically invoke it based on tool metadata.
* Expose the Knowledge Base as an MCP tool with proper descriptions and metadata.

Action

* Design and implement the MCP wrapper after evaluating whether it can be prioritized earlier.

⸻

2. Prioritize MCP Scaffolding

Requirement

John requested the team to scope the effort of creating the MCP scaffolding earlier instead of waiting until after Azure migration.

Reason

* Start building AI workflows sooner.
* Enable early content creation.
* Reduce future implementation effort.

Action

* Estimate the implementation effort and evaluate moving the MCP work ahead in the roadmap.

⸻

3. Authorization-Based Knowledge Updates

Requirement

Knowledge Base updates must follow PDP-based authorization.

Expected Workflow

* Document owners can directly update documents.
* Unauthorized users can only submit suggested changes.
* Suggestions should be routed to the document owner for approval.

⸻

4. GitHub Action + LangSmith Workflow

Requirement

Every Pull Request should automatically trigger an AI workflow.

Expected Flow
Pull Request
→ GitHub Action
→ LangSmith Workflow
→ Compare code changes with Knowledge Base
→ Generate documentation updates
→ Owner approval
→ Publish Knowledge Base

⸻

5. Faster Production Releases

Requirement

Since the Knowledge Base currently has very few users, John approved:

* Faster production deployments.
* Expedited hotfixes.
* No need to wait for the regular release cycle for Knowledge Base fixes.

Goal
Increase adoption and collect user feedback faster.

⸻

